      "Critical impact parameter by capture bisection: 5.196152423 M against 3√3 M, relative error 2.3e-12 (examples/02_validation.py, fresh run).",
      "Conserved-quantity drift over 5000 M of proper time on a tilted eccentric orbit: 1.2e-10 in total angular momentum and 4.0e-11 in the Hamiltonian constraint, against a test tolerance of 1e-8.",
      "Measured shadow edge equals the analytic arcsin(b_crit √f / r) to 1e-6 at 5°, 45°, and 90° camera inclination, in both image axes. Photo 3 is that check drawn out: the dashed analytic circle sits on the traced shadow at 55°, and the checkerboard sky shows the lensing.",
      "Weak-field light bending: at b = 1000 M the traced deflection is 0.004011824 rad against 4M/b = 0.004, and the excess over 4M/b tracks the 15πM²/4b² second-order term (1.23× it at b = 20 M, 1.004× at b = 1000 M).",
      "Face-on disk redshift from ray-traced photons matches √(1 − 3M/r) to 1e-6. Photo 4 shows the integrator's 3D precessing orbits; the tests hold a 40° tilted circular orbit at r = 8 M constant to 1e-7 in r over 3000 M of proper time (about 27 orbits) with its plane normal fixed to 1e-9.",
